{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01138",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.57,
      "end_seconds": 3.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Good morning. I've just opened your notes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.15,
      "end_seconds": 12.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Hello. I hope I'm not late."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.26,
      "end_seconds": 16.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Okay, lovely day outside, isn't it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.89,
      "end_seconds": 22.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "It is, I almost forgot I was coming here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.43,
      "end_seconds": 25.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "What's been worrying you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.11,
      "end_seconds": 35.96,
      "duration_seconds": 9.85,
      "text": "I wanted to get numbness in my feet looked at. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.43,
      "end_seconds": 42.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "How long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.5,
      "end_seconds": 47.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Probably one week. Yeah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.47,
      "end_seconds": 54.91,
      "duration_seconds": 5.44,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.56,
      "end_seconds": 62.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "It happens a few times a day. It's mild, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.66,
      "end_seconds": 65.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Any other symptoms with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.01,
      "end_seconds": 80.45,
      "duration_seconds": 13.44,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get being unsteady in the dark as well. As for being unsteady in the dark, it settles a little with holding on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.19,
      "end_seconds": 94.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Any weakness, back pain or bladder problems?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.15,
      "end_seconds": 99.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "No, no weakness, back pain or bladder problems."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.05,
      "end_seconds": 105.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "Okay, go on. How are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.97,
      "end_seconds": 107.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Nothing else aches."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.24,
      "end_seconds": 125.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.65,
      "end_seconds": 131.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.47,
      "text": "Diclofenac. I come out in... well, swelling of my lips."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.01,
      "end_seconds": 151.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.35,
      "end_seconds": 157.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "I've had diabetes for about a year now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.28,
      "end_seconds": 168.86,
      "duration_seconds": 9.58,
      "text": "Okay, I can see diabetes in your file as well. Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.62,
      "end_seconds": 181.33,
      "duration_seconds": 11.71,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning. I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours. My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.59,
      "end_seconds": 186.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.47,
      "end_seconds": 192.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "Glimepiride, 2 milligrams, maybe, before breakfast for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.94,
      "end_seconds": 197.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Do you have the packet or the prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.59,
      "end_seconds": 202.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.82,
      "end_seconds": 206.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Any surgery in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.98,
      "end_seconds": 217.48,
      "duration_seconds": 9.5,
      "text": "I had keyhole surgery on my gallbladder two years back. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.25,
      "end_seconds": 221.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.07,
      "end_seconds": 223.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "My grandmother had dementia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.26,
      "end_seconds": 228.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "Time for your numbers, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.84,
      "end_seconds": 240.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.05,
      "end_seconds": 262.61,
      "duration_seconds": 13.56,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 125 over 77, BMI works out to 24.7. And temperature 36.9, weight 79 kilos, oxygen saturation is 98 percent, height 179 centimetres, pulse 78."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 263.3,
      "end_seconds": 264.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.21,
      "end_seconds": 267.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "That's fine, I'll explain it soon."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.0,
      "end_seconds": 272.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.64,
      "end_seconds": 275.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.8,
      "end_seconds": 289.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.8,
      "text": "The ankle reflexes are reduced and the feeling is dulled below the knees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.38,
      "end_seconds": 318.38,
      "duration_seconds": 23.0,
      "text": "All finished, thank you. So, based on the history and the examination, it points towards a peripheral neuropathy, probably related to diabetes. Let me repeat that back to make sure. You've had numbness in your feet for one week, mild, and no weakness or back pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 320.11,
      "end_seconds": 321.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Mm, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.08,
      "end_seconds": 348.27,
      "duration_seconds": 25.19,
      "text": "Let's book an HbA1c to look into diabetes. Let's book a B12 level to look into neuropathy. For this, amitriptyline, 10 milligrams, at night, long term. You take it by mouth. That should help with nerve pain. Check both feet daily and wear well-fitting shoes. I think the neurology clinic should see you too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 349.22,
      "end_seconds": 349.92,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 350.79,
      "end_seconds": 358.89,
      "duration_seconds": 8.1,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 360.53,
      "end_seconds": 362.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.1,
      "end_seconds": 366.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Do get help quickly if the symptoms get worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.14,
      "end_seconds": 369.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Thank you, that's clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.47,
      "end_seconds": 374.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 375.55,
      "end_seconds": 377.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Thank you, that's helpful."
    }
  ]
}